        "id": 1000353
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T19:41:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The existing types   cannot be used as D-Bus return types.\nsdbusplus uses the D-Bus type system, which maps to sd-bus wire types. It can only serialise types it knows how to encode. \n\nWe need this because Every element maps cleanly to a D-Bus wire type: \nstd::map → a{...}, \nBinaryVector → ay, \nstd::string → s, \nuint64_t → t. \nThe std::variant here is a discriminated union that sdbusplus encodes as a D-Bus variant v. \nNo unordered_map, no size_t, no monostate.",
      "parentUuid": "7f44b085_68dadd1e",
      "revId": "d76f6a1cee4ff782888af4e2802290f9a9c857eb",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4101360_da4a5f1d",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/include/types.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000522
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T07:17:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With existing type I meant, why not use \"DbusVariantType\" which is already defined in the file as this new definition is subset of that.\nOnly downside I see is that, the already defined one has way more other options which will not be required for our use case.\nAnyways, lets go ahead with this new change.",
      "parentUuid": "62be6a57_c5ac6268",
      "revId": "d76f6a1cee4ff782888af4e2802290f9a9c857eb",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
